  "caveats": [
    "BH01 is healthy plasma cfDNA from Snyder 2016; TCGA-LIHC is liver HCC tissue \u2014 these are biologically distinct (cfDNA is fragmented cell-free DNA from dying cells; tissue is intact cellular DNA from resected tumor). The comparison is qualitative, not direct.",
    "FinaleMe outputs \u03b2 in [0,1]; TCGA HM450 sesame \u03b2 is in [0,1]; both are uncalibrated against each other. Spearman captures rank-order agreement only.",
    "Illumina HM450 manifest uses hg18 coordinates for MAPINFO; we liftOver to hg19 to match FinaleMe hg19 predictions.",
    "GDC TCGA-LIHC HM450 files were processed by the SeSAMe workflow (dc9467b78cf5); probe-level \u03b2 normalisation is independent of the FinaleMe HMM.",
    "Healthy plasma \u03b2 on a per-CpG basis is dominated by peripheral blood mononuclear cells; liver tissue \u03b2 from TCGA reflects hepatocytes + tumor stroma \u2014 different cell-type composition is the dominant source of disagreement.",
    "FinaleMe chr22 coverage here is a single sample (BH01); no technical replicates were decoded. n=1 makes any sample-level correlation noisy.",
    "A rigorous validation would require paired plasma samples with matched tissue methylation \u2014 currently we have neither (BH01 is published cfDNA, not paired with tissue)."
  ],
